DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261206
SUMMARY:HANDEL + HENDRIX With Dither\, R.B. Schlather\, and Ruckus
LOCATION:National Sawdust\, 80 N 6th St\, Brooklyn\, NY 11249
DESCRIPTION:Two radical innovators. Three centuries apart. One evening. Han
 del and Hendrix lived in adjacent homes in London's Mayfair district — s
 eparated by 250 years\, divided by a single wall\, now joined as the Hande
 l Hendrix House museum. In honor of the museum's 25th anniversary\, Nation
 al Sawdust and Handel Hendrix House America present an evening that brings
  these two radical innovators into direct confrontation. Electric guitar q
 uartet Dither open the evening with newly commissioned works that channel 
 Hendrix's experimental language. Director R.B. Schlather and early music e
 nsemble Ruckus then bring Handel's Deidamia — his final opera — to cha
 mber scale in National Sawdust's intimate acoustic space.\nhttps://www.nat
 ionalsawdust.org/event/handel-hendrix-with-dither-r-b-schlather-and-ruckus
 -12-5-26\nFrom Pushpin NYC: https://pushpin.city/nyc/
URL:https://www.nationalsawdust.org/event/handel-hendrix-with-dither-r-b-sc
 hlather-and-ruckus-12-5-26
END:VEVENT
